# entire review redesign — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` (if subagents available) or `superpowers:executing-plans` to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Restructure `entire review` around subcommands + role-based agent assignment + live tokens + inline prompts. Replace the multi-click first-run setup, derive the fix agent from roles (drop the "Choose fix agent" prompt), surface live token counts during runs, and add an inline `[Y]es · [s]elect fixes · [n]o · [A]lways` prompt at the end of every review.

**Architecture:**
- New `entire review setup` cobra subcommand owns first-run + edit-config. Two-step picker: pick a role for each installed agent (Reviewer / Fixer / Both / Skip), then pick skills only for Reviewer/Both.
- `entire review` becomes a runner with no inline picker: errors with `Run: entire review setup` if unconfigured. Adds an inline per-run prompt ask (`--prompt "..."` bypasses) and an inline fix prompt after review finishes.
- Settings schema gains a `role` field per agent in `ReviewConfig`. `ReviewFixAgent` becomes derived from roles (kept for one release as a migration source, then dropped).
- Claude/Codex reviewers emit `Tokens` events on every stream envelope that carries `usage`, not just at end-of-run.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, github.com/spf13/cobra, charm.land/huh/v2, github.com/go-git/go-git/v6, github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/{review, settings, agent}.

**Design reference:** `~/Desktop/entire-review-design.html` (saved 2026-05-20) — 8-scene click-through mockup of the chosen flow. Hand this to the implementing subagent for visual context.

---

## File Structure

**Modify:**
- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` — add `Role` type + constants, add `Role` field to `ReviewConfig`, add `FixAfterReview` field to `EntireSettings`, update JSON merging in `mergeRawSettings`.
- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go` — extend roundtrip tests for the new fields.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go` — drop the first-run auto-picker branch in `runReview`; add `--prompt` flag, inline per-run-prompt ask, inline post-run fix prompt; wire `setup` subcommand; drop multi-agent picker dispatch (roles handle that).
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker.go` — replace `RunReviewConfigPicker` with the new role-first flow; drop `pickReviewFixAgentPreference` and friends; drop `ConfirmFirstRunSetup` (no auto-launch).
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go` — accept `--prompt` flag; derive fix agent from roles; drop the spawn-time fix-agent picker; consolidate the "Run later" footer into a single `Run:` block with three pointers.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/multipicker.go` — **delete** (the multi-agent picker is obsolete; roles answer "which agents review" up front).
- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go` — emit `Tokens{}` on every envelope carrying `usage` (not only on `result`).
- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go` — emit `Tokens{}` whenever a codex envelope reports running usage (not only `turn.completed`).
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go` and `run_multi.go` — orchestrator changes are minimal; the new `Tokens` cadence is consumed by existing sinks unchanged.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review_bridge.go` — drop the bridge for the legacy fix-agent picker; wire the new `setup` subcommand through `Deps`.
- `CLAUDE.md` — update the `entire review` section to describe the new surface, role model, and inline prompts.

**Create:**
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/setup.go` — `RunSetup` function (the body of `entire review setup`).
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/setup_test.go` — picker validation, role normalization, save behavior.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/roles.go` — small package-private helpers: `NormalizeRoles`, `MigrateLegacyRoles`, `ReviewersOf`, `FixerOf`.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/roles_test.go` — table-driven tests for the helpers.
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/inline_prompt.go` — `ReadSingleKey` helper for `[Y]es · [s] · [n] · [A]`-style one-keypress prompts (raw mode on stdin, with non-TTY fallback that returns the default).
- `cmd/entire/cli/review/inline_prompt_test.go` — tests with stub stdin and non-TTY fallback assertions.

**Note on tests:**
- All new tests call `t.Parallel()` unless they mutate process-global state (env, cwd).
- Tests that touch git state use `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)` per CLAUDE.md.
- Subprocesses spawned from tests use `execx.NonInteractive` per CLAUDE.md.

---

