- [ ] **Step 3: Replace the first-run branch in `runReview` (with non-interactive auto-bootstrap)**

When `entire review` is invoked non-interactively (e.g., from inside Claude Code or Codex), we cannot drive the interactive `entire review setup` form. Rather than erroring with "Run: ..." (which a calling agent can't act on), auto-bootstrap a sensible default config: every launchable installed agent → Reviewer, alphabetically-first launchable → Fixer, skills = each agent's curated built-ins. Persist to settings (via `settings.Save` from Chunk 1) and proceed with the run. Print a one-line note explaining what was assumed.

Interactive callers (real TTY) still get the "Run: entire review setup" pointer — they can drive the setup form themselves.

Replace `cmd.go:240-254` with:

```go
if s == nil || len(s.Review) == 0 {
    if interactive.CanPromptInteractively() {
        cmd.SilenceUsage = true
        fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), "Not configured yet.")
        fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr())
        fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), "Run: entire review setup")
        return silentErr(errors.New("review not configured"))
    }
    // Non-interactive auto-bootstrap.
    bootstrapped, bErr := autoBootstrapReviewConfig(ctx, installed)
    if bErr != nil {
        cmd.SilenceUsage = true
        fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), "Cannot auto-configure review:", bErr)
        fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), "Hint: from an interactive shell, run `entire review setup`.")
        return silentErr(bErr)
    }
    if s == nil { s = &settings.EntireSettings{} }
    s.Review = bootstrapped
    if err := settings.Save(ctx, s); err != nil {
        // Persistence is best-effort — agents may run in environments
        // where settings paths are read-only. Continue with in-memory config.
        logging.Warn(ctx, "auto-bootstrap could not persist settings",
            slog.String("error", err.Error()))
    }
    fmt.Fprintln(out, formatAutoBootstrapNote(bootstrapped))
}
```

- [ ] **Step 4: Implement `autoBootstrapReviewConfig`**

In `setup.go` (since it shares helpers with the interactive flow):

```go
// autoBootstrapReviewConfig builds a default review map when no config
// exists and we cannot prompt the user. Every launchable installed
// agent that has curated built-in review skills becomes a Reviewer;
// the alphabetically-first launchable agent additionally becomes the
// Fixer (Role = Both). Returns an error if no agent qualifies — the
// caller must surface a clear hint to the user.
func autoBootstrapReviewConfig(ctx context.Context, installed []types.AgentName) (map[string]settings.ReviewConfig, error) {
    if len(installed) == 0 {
        return nil, errors.New("no agents installed (run `entire enable` first)")
    }
    var launchable []string
    for _, a := range installed {
        if _, ok := agent.LauncherFor(a); ok {
            launchable = append(launchable, string(a))
        }
    }
    if len(launchable) == 0 {
        return nil, errors.New("no launchable agents installed")
    }
    sort.Strings(launchable)
    out := make(map[string]settings.ReviewConfig, len(launchable))
    for i, name := range launchable {
        cfg := settings.ReviewConfig{Role: settings.RoleReviewer}
        if i == 0 { cfg.Role = settings.RoleBoth } // first one fixes too
        // Seed curated built-ins; empty if the agent has none.
        for _, b := range skilldiscovery.CuratedBuiltinsFor(name) {
            cfg.Skills = append(cfg.Skills, b.Name)
        }
        out[name] = cfg
    }
    return out, nil
}

// formatAutoBootstrapNote returns a one-line summary for the user.
func formatAutoBootstrapNote(review map[string]settings.ReviewConfig) string {
    reviewers := ReviewersOf(&settings.EntireSettings{Review: review})
    fixer := FixerOf(&settings.EntireSettings{Review: review})
    return fmt.Sprintf(
        "Auto-configured review (no prior config detected). Reviewers: %s. Fixer: %s. "+
            "Run `entire review setup` from an interactive shell to customize.",
        strings.Join(reviewers, ", "), fixer,
    )
}
```

